Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:50:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix missing <cstdint> include

Explicitly include <cstdint> in transaction_db_mutex.h, which
uses int64_t without including its defining header.

This avoids relying on transitive header dependencies and fixes
the build on musl-based systems.

For example, release 7 failed with:

> include/rocksdb/utilities/transaction_db_mutex.h:35:29: error: 'int64_t' has not been declared
>    35 |   virtual Status TryLockFor(int64_t timeout_time) = 0;
>       |                             ^~~~~~~
> include/rocksdb/utilities/transaction_db_mutex.h:12:1: note: 'int64_t' is defined in header '<cstdint>'; this is probably fixable by adding '#include <cstdint>'
>    11 | #include "rocksdb/status.h"
>   +++ |+#include <cstdint>
>    12 |

The current version builds successfully only because other
headers happen to include <cstdint> indirectly.

Signed-off-by: Z. Liu <zhixu.liu@gmail.com>

diff --git a/include/rocksdb/utilities/transaction_db_mutex.h b/include/rocksdb/utilities/transaction_db_mutex.h
index 751d3c9ee..7f47332c4 100644
--- a/include/rocksdb/utilities/transaction_db_mutex.h
+++ b/include/rocksdb/utilities/transaction_db_mutex.h
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 
 #pragma once
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <memory>
 
 #include "rocksdb/status.h"
-- 
